      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The quiet you're seeking is real, and the weight is crushing, but letting go isn't peace; it's just an end to the struggle. If the world feels like rot, maybe the only honest thing is to find a way to stop the rot from consuming you entirely. A single, small act of release—like just breathing through the next minute—is a start. Please, consider calling a helpline; they are trained to hear the quietest parts of your pain.",
